<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:16:Real Mode">
<!--
    kuna #1180: rejoining split conditions left an exit phi with three inputs
    after its CFG lost one predecessor, then calc_nz_mask indexed a third edge.
    P8 conditional joining must discover and repair every exit phi even when
    stack analysis has rewritten an earlier phi into arithmetic in place.
    This is an unconditional correctness fix with no P0 option.

    Independently assembled 16-bit probe (nasm -f bin, org 0x1000):
      push es; jnz join; call helper; mul bx; jbe finish
      join: mov dl,[es:bx]; jcxz finish
      repeat: loop repeat
      finish: mov ax,[cs:0xba72]; ret
      helper: ret
    The call, stack change, shared finish and loop exercise the reported failing
    path without bytes from Dazzle. Before the fix decompilation panics; the
    assertions require a complete body with its loop and final memory read.

    Pass one pins option segmentize off, where asserts 2-4 read the stack and
    memory accesses as segment() calls; pass two is the default (see
    kuna-segmentize.xml), where the final read folds to the global dat_ba72
    and both returned words survive (asserts 6-7).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1000">
067507e81000f7e37607268a17e302e2fe2ea172bac3c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1000" name="late_phi"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1016" name="helper"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option segmentize off</com>
  <com>lo fu late_phi</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option segmentize on</com>
  <com>lo fu late_phi</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="nodejoin #1: shared exit emits a complete body in both passes" min="2" max="2">late_phi\(</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="nodejoin #2: the loop survives the shared-exit repair" min="1" max="1">for \(; v2; v2 = v2 \+ -1\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="nodejoin #3: the final memory read remains in the body" min="1" max="1">segment\(0,0xba72\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="nodejoin #4: the returned high and low words survive" min="1" max="1">return CONCAT22\(v3,\*v1\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="nodejoin #5: the pipeline does not abort" min="0" max="0">Skipping|LOSS-131</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="nodejoin #6: with the default segmentize the loop survives the shared-exit repair" min="1" max="1">for \(; v1; v1 = v1 \+ -1\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="nodejoin #7: with the default segmentize the final read is the global and both returned words survive" min="1" max="1">^  return CONCAT22\(v2,dat_ba72\);$</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
